etwide dungeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quite fair point indeed. That said, if there's one thing the Martian desert has in great abundance is sand, making closed waterways with literal glass ceilings, plain or stained , a quite viable and aesthetically distinctive possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-29-2023, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T07:04:14-07:00","id":1506946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rebecca Ashlin\u0261</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/1286042-canals-vs-qanats#post1286042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While open canals are emblematic of Martian planetary romance, qanats, closed waterways, are probably more practical. It cuts down on evaporation of precious water and avoids the Martian desert silting them up. Besides which, a planetary network of closed tunnels is a planetwide dungeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea! I\u2019m gonna use this if I ever run Cavaliers of Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-am